    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d154">

                <pb facs="0324" n="306" xml:id="pg306"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">493.9283/10–1851: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Thailand</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Turner</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bangkok</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-10-18T15:00:00+07:00">October 18, 1951—3
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>913. Re Deptel 821, October 9, rptd Rangoon
                        334.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d154-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>
                    FonMin confirmed to me today reports
                    mentioned reftel that smuggling arms thru
                    Thai to KMT troops Burma has already ceased. He
                    stated that Thai Govt had issued strict instructions to Min Interior<anchor
                        n="2" xml:id="d154-f2"/> to prevent such smuggling, and that he expected be
                    able give me soon further details of measures being taken in this direction.</p>
                <p>Sent Dept 913, rptd Rangoon 934.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Turner</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d154-f1" n="1" xml:id="d154-f1-content">
                <p>In telegram 821 to Bangkok, October 9, the Embassy was asked to confirm reports
                    that the smuggling of arms and equipment to the KMT troops in Burma had ceased. The Embassy in Rangoon had
                    initiated this request in order to pass this information along to the Burmese
                    Foreign Office if these reports were true. (493.9283/9–1951)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d154-f2" n="2" xml:id="d154-f2-content">
                <p>Lt. Gen. Mangkorn Phrom Yodhi.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
